node_modules/

# package-lock.json IS tracked. It used to be ignored, which meant every
# `gcloud functions deploy` re-resolved `^1.7` and `^11` from the registry at
# build time: a compromised upstream release would have gone straight into a
# function that holds the Earth Engine service-account key. The lockfile is
# the only thing that makes a deploy reproducible, and `npm audit` has
# something to read.
